#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Script one Android app on one device.

A manual-capture yaml and a regression flow are two command sets. This
process never drives a second device. capture-manual-screenshots starts two
copies when a capture needs a phone and a tablet. A regression flow records
what the screen showed. It does not decide whether that result passed.

  ./script-android-app --check
  ./script-android-app --serial SERIAL [--form phone|tablet] [--locales all|TAG] [--shots GROUP,FILE] [--replace]
  ./script-android-app --check --flow FILE
  ./script-android-app --serial SERIAL --flow FILE [--var k=v] [--run-dir DIR]

--check does not touch adb. A flow run writes its report under --run-dir,
or under the sandbox, and never under /tmp.
"""
